# Bash reads these files on Linux and in WSL, where a CRLF shebang or a trailing \r in
# `set -euo pipefail` is a syntax error; core.autocrlf=true would otherwise hand out CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
# `git apply` compares a patch's context lines against the pinned dependency byte for byte,
# and those clones are LF; a CRLF patch fails on the first hunk.
*.patch text eol=lf
